---
// The system on one picture, drawn narrow so it stays legible on a 320 px phone, with the same facts as a list beside it.
// Colours come from the --diagram-* tokens in custom.css, so it follows the light and dark themes.
interface Props {
	/** Prefixes the SVG's element IDs, so the diagram can appear on more than one page. */
	id?: string;
}
const { id = 'architecture' } = Astro.props;
const arrow = `${id}-arrow`;
---

<div class="frame not-content">
<figure class="architecture">
	<svg
		viewBox="0 0 320 484"
		role="img"
		aria-labelledby={`${id}-title ${id}-desc`}
		xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
	>
		<title id={`${id}-title`}>How go-api-boilerplate fits together</title>
		<desc id={`${id}-desc`}>
			A browser and third-party OAuth apps reach the system through one web gateway on port 8080, which serves the
			web app and forwards /api/auth/ to the auth service and /api/user/ to the user service. Auth calls user's
			LoginService over Connect to redeem login codes; user fetches auth's JWKS to verify access tokens. Each
			service keeps its own store, memory, MySQL or MongoDB. The user service's outbox relay sends mail to
			Mailpit locally, or to any SMTP server.
		</desc>
		<defs>
			<marker id={arrow} viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" class="head"></path>
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<g class="box">
			<rect x="8" y="8" width="120" height="40" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="68" y="33" class="name">Browser</text>
		</g>
		<g class="box">
			<rect x="192" y="8" width="120" height="40" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="252" y="33" class="name">OAuth app</text>
		</g>
		<path d="M68 48v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<path d="M252 48v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>

		<g class="box">
			<rect x="8" y="88" width="304" height="56" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="160" y="112" class="name">web gateway :8080</text>
			<text x="160" y="132" class="note">the app, /api/auth/ and /api/user/</text>
		</g>
		<path d="M68 144v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<path d="M252 144v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>

		<g class="box service">
			<rect x="8" y="184" width="120" height="84" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="68" y="208" class="name">auth</text>
			<text x="68" y="230" class="note">sessions, OAuth2</text>
			<text x="68" y="249" class="note">and JWKS</text>
		</g>
		<g class="box service">
			<rect x="192" y="184" width="120" height="84" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="252" y="208" class="name">user</text>
			<text x="252" y="230" class="note">event-sourced</text>
			<text x="252" y="249" class="note">login codes</text>
		</g>
		<path d="M128 214h62" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<text x="160" y="206" class="label">Connect</text>
		<path d="M192 240h-62" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<text x="160" y="260" class="label">JWKS</text>

		<path d="M68 268v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<path d="M252 268v38" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>

		<g class="box store">
			<path d="M8 316a60 8 0 0 1 120 0v66a60 8 0 0 1-120 0z"></path>
			<path d="M8 316a60 8 0 0 0 120 0" class="rim"></path>
			<text x="68" y="348" class="name">auth store</text>
			<text x="68" y="368" class="note">clients, grants</text>
		</g>
		<g class="box store">
			<path d="M192 316a60 8 0 0 1 120 0v66a60 8 0 0 1-120 0z"></path>
			<path d="M192 316a60 8 0 0 0 120 0" class="rim"></path>
			<text x="252" y="345" class="name">user store</text>
			<text x="252" y="364" class="note">events, users</text>
			<text x="252" y="381" class="note">and outbox</text>
		</g>

		<path d="M252 392v34" class="line" marker-end={`url(#${arrow})`}></path>
		<text x="244" y="414" class="label end">outbox relay</text>

		<g class="box">
			<rect x="192" y="428" width="120" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
			<text x="252" y="449" class="name">Mailpit</text>
			<text x="252" y="467" class="note">or your SMTP</text>
		</g>
		<text x="8" y="447" class="label start">One store per service:</text>
		<text x="8" y="466" class="label start">memory, MySQL or MongoDB</text>
	</svg>

	<ol class="legend">
		<li>
			<strong>One origin.</strong> The gateway serves the web app and forwards <code>/api/auth/</code> and
			<code>/api/user/</code>, so cookies stay SameSite and nothing needs CORS.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>auth</strong> issues every token and sets the only cookies. Clients and grants are plain rows: short-lived
			secrets don't belong in a permanent log.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>user</strong> is event-sourced. A change appends events, updates the <code>users</code> projection and
			queues its emails in one transaction.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>No call per request.</strong> Each API verifies access tokens itself with auth's JWKS, cached.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>One internal RPC.</strong> auth redeems login codes with user over Connect, on a listener the gateway
			doesn't expose.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Mail at least once.</strong> The outbox relay retries with backoff. Locally, Mailpit catches every
			message.
		</li>
	</ol>
</figure>
</div>

<style>
	/* The figure sits beside its legend only when its own column is wide enough, which on a docs
	   page with large text can be narrower than the viewport suggests. */
	.frame {
		container-type: inline-size;
	}

	.architecture {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin: 0;
	}

	svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 26rem;
		height: auto;
		margin-inline: auto;
		font-family: var(--__sl-font);
	}

	.box :is(rect, path:not(.rim)) {
		fill: var(--diagram-surface);
		stroke: var(--diagram-line);
		stroke-width: 1.25;
	}

	.box .rim {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--diagram-line);
		stroke-width: 1.25;
	}

	.service rect {
		stroke: var(--diagram-accent);
		stroke-width: 2;
	}

	text {
		text-anchor: middle;
	}

	.name {
		fill: var(--diagram-text);
		font-size: 15px;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.note,
	.label {
		fill: var(--diagram-muted);
		font-size: 12.5px;
	}

	.label.start {
		text-anchor: start;
	}

	.label.end {
		text-anchor: end;
	}

	.line {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--diagram-line);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}

	.head {
		fill: var(--diagram-line);
	}

	.legend {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	.legend strong {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}

	.legend code {
		padding: 0.0625rem 0.25rem;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-inline-code);
		font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.875em;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}

	@container (min-width: 46rem) {
		.architecture {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 26rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
